\begin{MintedVerbatim}[commandchars=\\\{\}]
Standing OUTSIDE the lambda:
    index 0 = x       ← k=0 means \PYGZdq{}replace x\PYGZdq{}
    index 1 = z       ← s=(bvar 1) means \PYGZdq{}insert z\PYGZdq{}

Standing INSIDE the lambda (which binds w):
    index 0 = w       ← the lambda\PYGZsq{}s own parameter (NEW)
    index 1 = x       ← was index 0 from outside
    index 2 = z       ← was index 1 from outside
\end{MintedVerbatim}
